@page "/docs/tools/vs-code-preview"

@* Preview with Hot Reload (0.9.4: out/preview.js, framing.js). The app runs with dotnet watch; the panel loads it
   through a local relay that drops the headers forbidding frames. The library sets nothing for it: the request for
   IZZYBLAZOR_PREVIEW=1 was declined (Nov 26, 2026), since the relay removes the header. *@

<ArticlePage Section="tools" Slug="vs-code-preview">
    <Lead>
        Preview with Hot Reload runs your app and shows the page you're editing beside its code, at a phone's,
        a tablet's or the panel's width. Use it to see a page at each size as you write it.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Start it</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Choose Preview with Hot Reload in the title bar of a <Code>.razor</Code> page, in its right-click
            menu, or under Project, in Run. The extension starts the app with <Code>dotnet watch</Code> and
            opens the page beside the editor. The status bar shows the app while it runs. Stop the app, in the
            preview's bar, ends it. For a route with a parameter, type the address in the preview's bar.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Sizes</Heading>
        <Table Items="Sizes" Caption="The preview's sizes" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Size" Width="Length.Rem(8)">@context!.Name</TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="The page is">@context!.Text</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>
        <TextBlock>
            The page is drawn at the device's real width and scaled to fit the panel, so your breakpoints apply
            as they would on the device. Rotate turns a phone or a tablet to landscape.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">As you edit</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            When you save, the page reloads as soon as hot reload has applied the change, and keeps its scroll
            position. When a change needs a restart, the page reloads once the app is back. A page with
            WebAssembly components isn't reloaded: <Code>dotnet watch</Code> changes it in place.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            With Follow editor on, the preview moves to the page you open in the editor. Links in the preview
            work, and the preview's bar shows the address you are at. You can type another address, or open
            the page in your browser.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">How the page is loaded</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            ASP.NET Core forbids framing a page that has a form: its antiforgery token comes with the header
            <Code>X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN</Code>. The preview loads the app through a small relay on your
            machine, which removes that header and a <Code>frame-ancestors</Code> rule, and adds a script that
            reloads the page and reports its address. Your app isn't changed, and Open in Browser goes straight
            to it. When the preview stays blank, open the page in your browser.
        </TextBlock>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private sealed record Row(string Name, string Text);

    private static readonly Row[] Sizes =
    [
        new("Phone", "390 by 844 pixels."),
        new("Tablet", "768 by 1024 pixels."),
        new("Desktop", "As wide as the panel."),
    ];
}
